{"name":"Mount Olive","hex":"#716646","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Mount Olive","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A locality in the Oberon council area, eastern New South Wales, Australia.","A locality in the Singleton council area, eastern New South Wales, Australia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Mount_Olive"}],"entries":[{"title":"Smithfield, Toronto","blocks":[{"text":"Smithfield is a neighbourhood and former village in Toronto, Ontario, Canada. Some new residents of Toronto and new immigrants to Canada are attracted to this neighbourhood, mainly because there is a large amount of affordable public housing. It is named after the former village of Smithfield located at the intersection of Albion Road and Martin Grove Road. The neighbourhood is located north of the west branch of the Humber River and west of Kipling Avenue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Mount_Olive-Silverstone-Jamestown_from_Kipling.jpg/330px-Mount_Olive-Silverstone-Jamestown_from_Kipling.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smithfield%2C_Toronto"},{"title":"Line 6 Finch West","blocks":[{"text":"Line 6 Finch West, also known as the Finch West LRT, is a light rail transit line in Toronto, Ontario, Canada. Operated by the Toronto Transit Commission (TTC) as part of the Toronto subway, the 10.3-kilometre (6.4 mi), 18-stop line extends from Finch West station on Line 1 Yonge–University at Keele Street to Humber College station at the North Campus of Humber Polytechnic in the district of Etobicoke. The line operates in a dedicated at-grade right-of-way segregated from street traffic, much of it within the median of Finch Avenue West. It uses standard gauge rather than the broad Toronto gauge used by the three older heavy rail subway lines."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/ACS_Train_Arriving_At_Humber_College_Station_%283-2_cropped%29.jpg/330px-ACS_Train_Arriving_At_Humber_College_Station_%283-2_cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Line_6_Finch_West"},{"title":"Olive","blocks":[{"text":"The cultivated olive is a subspecies of subtropical evergreen tree in the family Oleaceae. Modern cultivars are traced primarily to the Near East, Aegean Sea, and Strait of Gibraltar. Olea europaea is the type species for its genus, Olea, which lends its name to the Oleaceae plant family. The olive fruit is classed botanically as a drupe, similar in structure and function to the cherry or peach. The term oil was originally synonymous with olive oil."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Olivesfromjordan.jpg/330px-Olivesfromjordan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Olive"},{"title":"Olive (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Olive, also called olive green, is a dark shade of yellowish green, like that of unripe or green olives."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Olives_stuffed_with_almonds.jpg/330px-Olives_stuffed_with_almonds.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Olive_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Clairville_%26_Smithfield_aerial_view_2023.jpg/500px-Clairville_%26_Smithfield_aerial_view_2023.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Clairville_%26_Smithfield_aerial_view_2023.jpg/1280px-Clairville_%26_Smithfield_aerial_view_2023.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Clairville_%26_Smithfield_aerial_view_2023.jpg/500px-Clairville_%26_Smithf